.1077791303396225,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-0.0999358594417572,-0.41975608468055725,-0.7054146528244019,-6.794906312279636e-06,-0.016284428536891937,-0.012385714799165726,-3.099436753473128e-06,0.0,0.0,-3.576278118089249e-07,0.0,-3.576278118089249e-07,-1.1920928244535389e-07,0.0,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-7.152555099310121e-07,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-7.152555099310121e-07,0.0,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-1.1920928244535389e-07,0.0,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-0.2226700335741043,-1.035831093788147,-0.3473707437515259,-1.062025547027588,-0.025960637256503105,-0.0473032109439373,-0.06078886613249779,-0.008732583373785019,-0.010087225586175919,-0.023404881358146667,-2.3841830625315197e-06,-0.17716693878173828,0.0,0.0,-2.3841855067985307e-07,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-1.1920928244535389e-07,0.0,0.0,-2.312633478140924e-05,-4.207999518257566e-05,-1.1920928244535389e-07,0.0,-0.0006242233794182539,-1.3351351299206726e-05,-3.6954811548639555e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,10061,400,64,4779,400,65,4779,400,66,4779,323,400,67,3,387,6785,1931,5109,1741,429,400,18,21,64,488,220,19,65,488,220,19,66,488,220,18,67,284,220,17,20,2418,220,7379,279,7192,897,315,198,78045,64,1124,15136,1124,26888,90,65,92,1124,15136,1124,26888,58,18,15370,66,92,1124,15136,1124,26888,58,19,15370,67,92,7110,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nLet $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ and $d$ be positive real numbers such that $36a + 4b + 4c + 3d = 25.$  Find the maximum value of\n\\[a \\times \\sqrt{b} \\times \\sqrt[3]{c} \\times \\sqrt[4]{d}.\\]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"2de17349d2d1c86b044b03c314cdb17fa7aaf2bf8b169f36bc351ecf136830e7"},"seconds":55.60058236122131,"seed":103115638820728710,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the maximum value of \\(a \\times \\sqrt{b} \\times \\sqrt[3]{c} \\times \\sqrt[4]{d}\\) under the constraint \\(36a + 4b + 4c + 3d = 25\\), we can use the method of Lagrange multipliers or apply the AM-GM inequality. Here, we will use the AM-GM inequality for simplicity.\n\nThe AM-GM inequality states that for non-negative real numbers \\(x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n\\),\n\\[\n\\frac{x_1 + x_2 + \\cdots + x_n}{n} \\geq \\sqrt[n]{x_1 x_2 \\cdots x_n},\n\\]\nwith equality if and only if \\(x_1 = x_2 = \\cdots = x_n\\).\n\nLet's rewrite the constraint \\(36a + 4b + 4c + 3d = 25\\) in a form that allows us to apply AM-GM. Consider the expression \\(36a + 4b + 4c + 3d\\). We want to relate this to \\(a \\times \\sqrt{b} \\times \\sqrt[3]{c} \\times \\sqrt[4]{d}\\).\n\nUsing AM-GM inequality on the terms \\(36a, 4b, 4c, 3d\\), we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{36a + 4b + 4c + 3d}{4} \\geq \\sqrt[4]{36a \\cdot 4b \\cdot 4c \\cdot 3d}.\n\\]\nGiven \\(36a + 4b + 4c + 3d = 25\\), we can substitute:\n\\[\n\\frac{25}{4} \\geq \\sqrt[4]{36a \\cdot 4b \\cdot 4c \\cdot 3d}.\n\\]\nRaising both sides to the fourth power, we get:\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{25}{4}\\right)^4 \\geq 36a \\cdot 4b \\cdot 4c \\cdot 3d.\n\\]\nSimplifying the right-hand side, we have:\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{25}{4}\\right)^4 \\geq 1728abc^{1/3}d^{1/4}.\n\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\frac{390625}{256} \\geq 1728abc^{1/3}d^{1/4}.\n\\]\nTo isolate \\(a \\times \\sqrt{b} \\times \\sqrt[3]{c} \\times \\sqrt[4]{d}\\), we divide both sides by \\(1728\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{390625}{256 \\cdot 1728} \\geq abc^{1/3}d^{1/4}.\n\\]\nSimplifying the fraction, we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{390625}{442368} \\geq abc^{1/3}d^{1/4}.\n\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\frac{390625}{442368} = \\frac{15625}{17694.72} \\approx 0.883.\n\\]\nThus, the maximum value of \\(a \\times \\sqrt{b} \\times \\sqrt[3]{c} \\times \\sqrt[4]{d}\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{125}{144}}.\n\\]\n\nEquality in the AM-GM inequality holds when \\(36a = 4b = 4c = 3d\\). Solving these equations under the constraint \\(36a + 4b + 4c + 3d = 25\\) will confirm that the maximum value is indeed \\(\\boxed{\\frac{125}{144}}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{125}{144}}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
